// REJECTS: PLACEHOLDER
//
// `batchPersister: PERSISTER_BATCH BRACE_OPEN (persisterSink | targetShape | ingestMode)*
// BRACE_CLOSE` -- all three optional to the grammar, all three required by
// visitBatchPersister. Drop targetShape and what is left is a legal `Streaming` persister
// body plus an ingest mode.
//
// sink is checked first and targetShape second, so this file is what reaches the second
// check.
###Persistence
Persistence test::persistence::neg::BatchNoTargetShape
{
  doc: 'batch persister with no target shape';
  trigger: Manual;
  service: test::persistence::Service;
  persister: Batch
  {
    sink: Relational
    {
      database: test::persistence::Database;
    }
    ingestMode: NontemporalSnapshot
    {
      auditing: None;
    }
  }
}
